#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# framed

#% text
# `framed(x)` is x (a graphic, a plot or an expression) in a frame.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Options: `background` (a colour under it), `frame_style` (the frame's colour).

#% item
# The value is a `graphics` term.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A framed graphic:

#% cell
framed(graphics(disk()))
#% output
#= image("framed.files/framed-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A framed expression:

#% cell
framed(x^2 + 1)
#% output
#= image("framed.files/framed-2.svgz")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# A coloured frame and background:

#% cell
framed("note", frame_style: red, background: light_gray)
#% output
#= image("framed.files/framed-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `labeled`, `grid`, `inset`
